## Summary of Key Findings

| Aspect | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Client-side filtering** | TransactionsPage.tsx does all filtering **in-memory** after fetching all transactions. Searches by `senderName`, `receiverName`, `senderAccountNumber`, `receiverAccountNumber`. Filters by `status`. Date-range filtering also client-side. |
| **Client API call** | `fetchTransactionsAction(userId)` calls `GET /api/wallet/users/:userId/transactions` -- **no query parameters** sent. |
| **Server query endpoint** | `GET /users/:userId/transactions/query` accepts `status` (required: "success" or "failed") and optional `from`/`to` dates. **No text search.** |
| **Server list endpoint** | `GET /users/:userId/transactions` also exists but returns all transactions for a user with no filtering at all. |
| **Notifications** | No search/query endpoint. Only `limit` query param on list. No text search or status filtering. |
| **Accounts** | No search/query endpoint at all. Only CRUD by ID/number. |
| **Client notification types** | **None exist** -- no notification type in `client/src/types/`. |
